                <rubric>Notes</rubric>
                <paragraph>In order to support zen <reference internal="1" refuri="hydra_zen.builds#meta-field"><inline classes="std std-ref">meta-fields</inline></reference> and
                    <reference internal="1" refuri="hydra_zen.builds#zen-wrapper"><inline classes="std std-ref">zen wrappers</inline></reference>, hydra-zen redirects Hydra to an intermediary
                    function – <literal classes="xref py py-obj">hydra_zen.funcs.zen_processing</literal> – during instantiation; i.e.
                    <literal classes="xref py py-obj">zen_processing</literal> is made to be the <literal classes="xref py py-obj">_target_</literal> of the config and <literal classes="xref py py-obj">_zen_target</literal>
                    indicates the object that is ultimately being configured for instantiation.</paragraph>
                <rubric>Examples</rubric>
                <doctest_block classes="doctest" xml:space="preserve">&gt;&gt;&gt; from hydra_zen import builds, uses_zen_processing, to_yaml
&gt;&gt;&gt; ConfA = builds(dict, a=1)
&gt;&gt;&gt; ConfB = builds(dict, a=1, zen_partial=True)
&gt;&gt;&gt; ConfC = builds(dict, a=1, zen_wrappers=lambda x: x)
&gt;&gt;&gt; ConfD = builds(dict, a=1, zen_meta=dict(hidden_field=None))
&gt;&gt;&gt; ConfE = builds(dict, a=1, zen_meta=dict(hidden_field=None), zen_partial=True)
&gt;&gt;&gt; uses_zen_processing(ConfA)
False
&gt;&gt;&gt; uses_zen_processing(ConfB)
False
&gt;&gt;&gt; uses_zen_processing(ConfC)
True
&gt;&gt;&gt; uses_zen_processing(ConfD)
True
&gt;&gt;&gt; uses_zen_processing(ConfE)
True</doctest_block>
                <paragraph>Demonstrating the indirection that is used to facilitate zen-processing features.</paragraph>
